  "source_conclusions": [
    "The only true argument is explicit rt2&&!mb1 setup branch; default false preserves automatic recovery lifecycle. Whole application inverse matches exact parent, and ordinary setup/loop function comparison passes.",
    "Repository-owned exact pinned DCD/USBD/port generated copies append helpers. Removing helpers restores exact parent normal TU bases; no installed framework source change. Routing unit rejects omitted/duplicate/original objects. Final real link exclusion remains required.",
    "Core0/thread/PRIMASK/one-shot/initialized descriptor+IRQ+queue+driver preflight; global interrupt mask and successful nonblocking USB mutex acquisition quiesce core0 USB execution. Core1 remains boot-state Pending before handoff and has no USB work.",
    "Disable both existing USBCTRL and assigned task IRQ, disconnect, clear stale pending, existing SDK USBCTRL reset/DPRAM+register clear, EP0+noncontrol+allocator+SOF reset, original class/device/maps/control reset, empty existing event FIFO, clear pending, restore delivery, connect last. No new registration, IRQ claim, OSAL lock or queue allocation.",
    "All built-in reset callbacks execute; CDC coding/wanted_char and initialized locks intentionally retained. Existing XInput reset is empty and no XInput backend is constructed on manual route.",
    "75-byte existing CDC configuration, existing 2e8a:1092 Configurator identity and protocol retained; source descriptor builder allocation inspected. No descriptor/VID/PID redesign.",
    "Existing recovery inspection and backend read-only state precede restart and new pullup exposure. New USB helpers have no persistent-store references. Existing mutation guards/read-only store semantics remain unchanged.",
    "Preflight failure preserves old USB hardware; after reset failure remains detached/USB IRQs disabled, one-shot consumed and route permanently refuses backend service. No retry, new observer, forced SETUP, new manual IRQ pend, arbitrary delay, USB upgrade or root-cause claim."
  ],
